  "description": "meme-id: isis_murders_140_people_in_paris; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a graphic image of Paris at night with text claiming ISIS murdered 140 people on 11.13.2015 and that Paris closed its borders, followed by the sarcastic claim that Donald Trump's wall 'doesn't seem so stupid now does it?'. The intent is to use the trauma of a real-world terrorist attack to rhetorically justify or normalize a controversial political proposal (Trump's border wall) by implying that such a measure was 'obvious' or 'necessary' in light of the attack. This is harmful because it weaponizes a horrific event for political argumentation, potentially normalizing xenophobic or isolationist policies, and risks trivializing the victims of the attack by reducing their suffering to a political talking point. The meme does not target any specific protected group with hate or abuse, but it promotes a harmful political message by exploiting collective trauma.",
